{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[G]As the blackbird [A7]in the spring,
[D7]'Neath the willow [G]tree,
[G]Sat and piped, I [A7]heard him sing,
[D7]Sing of Aura [G]Lea.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Aura [B7]Lea, [Em]Aura [G7]Lea,
[C]Maid of [Cm]golden [G]hair;
[E7]Sunshine came a[A7]long with thee,
And [D7]swallows in the [G]air.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[G]In thy blush the [A7]rose was born,
[D7]Music, when you [G]spake,
[G]Through thine azure [A7]eye the morn,
[D7]Sparkling seemed to [G]break.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
